{"id":"n-20261009-o35ix4","category":"business","display_title":"Global Markets and Local Movements","display_title_he":"השווקים הגלובליים ותנועות מקומיות","short_summary":"Global markets react to tech sector fluctuations and statements regarding monetary policy and geopolitical tensions, while local Israeli companies see executive changes and stake increases.","english_level":"C1","words":579,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns%2C_average_across_the_surveyed_markets%2C_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png/960px-BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns%2C_average_across_the_surveyed_markets%2C_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"SOworu (WMF) · CC BY 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns,_average_across_the_surveyed_markets,_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001558969","title":"חמישה דברים שכדאי לדעת לקראת פתיחת המסחר בבורסה","published_at":"2026-10-09T05:36:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-09T05:36:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:22:47.341Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Financial markets recently experienced notable shifts, driven by developments in the technology sector, central bank commentary, and corporate updates. On Wall Street, major indices closed lower as technology shares dragged the market down. The Nasdaq dropped by roughly 1.3%, the S&P 500 softened by about 0.5%, and the Dow Jones managed to stay afloat with an increase of approximately 0.1%. According to reports from the Financial Times and CNBC, the downturn was largely triggered by disclosures regarding artificial intelligence giant OpenAI, which informed investors that its annual revenue run rate stood at 50 billion dollars in September, falling short of higher market projections. Despite this adjustment, technology analyst Gil Luria from D.A. Davidson expressed confidence in the sector, emphasizing that the substantial combined revenue of AI developers indicates robust commercial demand. He noted that the combined revenue of OpenAI and Anthropic, reaching a pace of 120 billion dollars compared to nearly zero two years prior, proves that companies and consumers are willing to pay for artificial intelligence.","In related technology news, D.A. Davidson significantly raised its price target for memory chip manufacturer Micron from 2,100 dollars to 3,000 dollars, reflecting an unusual upside of over 180 percent after the stock more than tripled its value since the beginning of the year. Luria cited surging long-term demand for memory to support complex artificial intelligence models, explaining that AI models yield better results, run faster, and possess longer context windows with more memory. Meanwhile, central bank officials maintained a hawkish stance on monetary policy. Federal Reserve Governor Christopher Waller indicated during a forum in the Bank of Turkey in Istanbul that additional interest rate adjustments will be necessary within a reasonable timeframe to curb stubborn inflation that has remained above the central bank's 2 percent target for over five years, though he suggested that hikes do not need to occur at consecutive meetings. Bond yields experienced volatility before retreating following robust demand at a 22 billion dollar 30-year Treasury auction and comments from President Trump confirming that the United States will refrain from military action against Iran prior to the November mid-term elections. Consequently, oil prices also pulled back from earlier highs, with Brent crude trading around 103 dollars a barrel and WTI crude around 90 dollars a barrel.","Domestically on the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange, which had closed the previous trading day in a mixed trend with the Tel Aviv 35 index down by about 0.2% and the Tel Aviv 90 index adding roughly 0.6%, notable leadership and ownership adjustments unfolded in the corporate sector. Yonatan Kaplan announced his departure from his position as chairman of the income-producing real estate company Vilar, owned by the Tisser family at 75.7%, after leading the firm for nine years starting from October 2017. During his tenure, Vilar achieved an 82 percent increase in its share price and now trades at a valuation of approximately 2.9 billion shekels, following the passing of former owner Shlomo Tisser and the transition of ownership to his family led by his widow Michal. Simultaneously, the Wertheim family expanded its financial footprint by acquiring additional shares in Mizrahi Tefahot Bank. Through purchases totaling 15.8 million shekels over a two-day period, the family increased its stake by just under 0.15% to reach 20.47 percent of the bank's shares, representing a valuation exceeding 11.8 billion shekels. As the local market faced negative arbitrage from Wall Street, including expected declines in chip stocks Tower and Nova alongside gains in Teva and Formula Systems, market participants continued to closely monitor upcoming macroeconomic indicators, particularly upcoming consumer and producer price index releases in the United States."],"facts":[{"fact":"Yonatan Kaplan, chairman of the income-producing real estate company Vilar, is stepping down after nine years in the role.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Vilar company is controlled by the Tisser family (75.7%), led by Michal Tisser following the passing of Shlomo Tisser.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"During Kaplan's tenure, Vilar's share price rose by 82%, and the company is currently traded at a value of 2.9 billion shekels.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Wertheim family increased its holdings in Mizrahi Tefahot Bank by purchasing shares worth a cumulative 15.8 million shekels over two days.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Wertheim family now holds 20.47% of Mizrahi Tefahot Bank, valued at over 11.8 billion shekels.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Wall Street experienced a sharp decline in technology stocks, with the Nasdaq falling 1.3%, the S&P 500 dropping 0.5%, and the Dow Jones rising 0.1%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The trigger for the tech sell-off was a Financial Times report revealing that OpenAI's annual revenue run rate was about $20 billion lower than market estimates, standing at $50 billion in September.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Analyst Gil Luria from D.A. Davidson noted that the combined revenue run rate of OpenAI and Anthropic reaching $120 billion demonstrates strong willingness to pay for AI.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"D.A. Davidson raised its price target for Micron to 3,000 dollars, reflecting significant upside based on growing memory demand for AI models.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Federal Reserve Governor Christopher Waller stated that additional interest rate hikes are needed to tame inflation above the 2% target, though not necessarily at consecutive meetings.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"President Trump stated that the United States will not attack Iran until after the mid-term elections in November, leading to a decline in oil prices and bond yields.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Financial","lemma":"financial","pos":"adj","he":"פיננסי","name":false},{"text":"markets","lemma":"market","pos":"n","he":"שוק","name":false},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"adv","he":"לאחרונה","name":false},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"v","he":"חווה","name":false},{"text":"notable","lemma":"notable","pos":"adj","he":"בולט","name":false},{"text":"shifts","lemma":"shift","pos":"n","he":"שינוי","name":false},{"text":"driven","lemma":"drive","pos":"v","he":"מונע","name":false},{"text":"developments","lemma":"development","pos":"n","he":"התפתחות","name":false},{"text":"technology","lemma":"technology","pos":"n","he":"טכנולוגיה",